From: "Brandon Barclay (AK6MJ)" <ak6mj@w7avm.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:33:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Respawn arecord/aplay when the sound card disappears

The module docstring says that if the codec disappears (USB unplug) "the
pipe closes and we just respawn on next start()", but nothing calls
start() again, and start() returned early because the dead process was
still recorded. After the radio was unplugged and plugged back in, the
panel kept running with no audio in either direction: RX was silent and
the browser's mic audio went into a dead pipe, until the service was
restarted. (On an IC-7100 the second symptom looked like a radio that
keys but modulates nothing: the TX meters stayed at idle.)

Each pipe now respawns its own arecord/aplay every 2 s after it dies
(RETRY_S), drops the audio that piled up meanwhile, and logs the loss
and the recovery once instead of on every retry.

Checked on an IC-7100: killing arecord and aplay by hand, both were back
within 6 s with the service still running. I have not repeated this with
a physical unplug after the change.

The tests simulate a pipe breaking (aplay) and arecord hitting EOF; both
fail against the previous code and pass now.
